# Firebase Patterns – AskmeHUMG

## Authentication (UC-1.1)

Google Sign-In accepts any Google account. After sign-in, upsert `users/{uid}` then check `isHumgVerified`:
- `isHumgVerified == false` → redirect to `/verify-humg-email` (OTP flow via Cloud Function + Resend)
- `isHumgVerified == true` → proceed to `/`

```dart
// Upsert users/{uid} with merge: true
await firestore.collection('users').doc(uid).set({
  'name': user.displayName ?? '',
  'email': user.email ?? '',
  'avatar': user.photoURL ?? '',
  'role': 'user',
  'createdAt': FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),
  'isBlocked': false,
  'isHumgVerified': false,
  'humgEmail': null,
}, SetOptions(merge: true));
```

## Firestore Write Patterns

### Batch Write — required for multi-collection writes

```dart
// UC-3.3: Answer a question
final batch = firestore.batch();
batch.set(answersCol.doc(), answerData);
batch.update(questionsCol.doc(questionId), {'status': 'answered'});
await batch.commit();

// UC-4.3: Comment — use a transaction so commentCount / hotScore stay consistent
// under concurrent comments (see firebase_feed_datasource.postComment).
```

### Like Toggle (UC-4.2)

```dart
// Transaction: rewrite likedBy, set likeCount == likedBy.length, recompute hotScore.
// (arrayUnion + increment alone drift if data was inconsistent.)
```

### Cursor Pagination (UC-4.1)

```dart
// UC-4.1 default: trending (hotScore). Chronological (createdAt) is fallback only.
Query query = firestore
    .collection('answers')
    .where('isPublished', isEqualTo: true)
    .orderBy('hotScore', descending: true)
    .limit(20);
if (lastDoc != null) query = query.startAfterDocument(lastDoc);
```

## Anonymous Question (UC-3.1)

Always attach App Check token before calling Cloud Function:

```dart
final token = await FirebaseAppCheck.instance.getToken(false);
await dio.post('/submitQuestion',
  data: {'toUserId': toUserId, 'content': content},
  options: Options(headers: {'X-Firebase-AppCheck': token}),
);
```

Client validates: `content.length ∈ [1, 300]` before sending.

## Admin Check

```dart
// Via Custom Claims (preferred)
final claims = (await user.getIdTokenResult()).claims;
final isAdmin = claims?['admin'] == true;
```
